#
# one_two_three(0) == [0, 0]
# one_two_three(1) == [1, 1]
# one_two_three(2) == [2, 11]
# one_two_three(3) == [3, 111]
# one_two_three(19) == [991, 1111111111111111111]
# And it should give the following results in Javascript, Scala, D, Go, Rust, C, and Java:
